# WiseEvidence — environment variable template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in real values for
# local development. NEVER commit `.env` or any real credential.
#
# Milestone 1 ships only the Supabase *connection strategy* — there is no
# database schema, migration, or table yet (see supabase/README.md). These
# public variables let the browser client be constructed; leaving them empty
# is fine for the static-first M1 site.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC — safe to expose to the browser (Astro exposes PUBLIC_* to the client).
# These are the anon-key pair protected by Row-Level Security in later milestones.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY — NEVER prefix with PUBLIC_, never send to the browser.
# The service-role key bypasses RLS and must stay server-side only.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Milestone 3 (Manual Research MVP) adds authenticated admin/reviewer workflows
# that run server-side. Leaving these empty keeps the site working (the admin
# data surfaces show a "not configured" notice — see docs/26 §25, the Supabase
# pending gate); fill them once a real Supabase project exists.

# Supabase project URL + anon key read server-side by the SSR auth client
# (cookie sessions). Same values as the PUBLIC_ pair above; duplicated without
# the PUBLIC_ prefix so they are NOT bundled into client code.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Service-role key — bypasses RLS. Used ONLY by privileged server writes
# (publication, audit). Never expose to the browser.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Direct PostgreSQL connection string for the server data-access executor.
# Server only. When absent, admin/data pages degrade to "not configured".
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI (Milestone 6) — SERVER-ONLY. NEVER prefix with PUBLIC_; never send to the
# browser; never commit a real key. When AI_PROVIDER is unset or "mock", the
# offline deterministic MockAIProvider is used and NO key/network is required —
# the free-first default (docs/29 §4). A real provider is opt-in below.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI_PROVIDER=mock                 # "mock" (default) | "openai-compatible"

# Real provider only (an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, e.g. OpenRouter — used later
# for the M6.1 benchmark in a secure environment). The key is read only in the
# server process and is never persisted in ai_job/ai_result or logs.
# AI_BASE_URL=
# AI_API_KEY=
# AI_MODEL=
# AI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=1024

# Operator-supplied pricing per 1,000,000 tokens, for cost derivation. If absent,
# recorded cost is NULL — never a guessed $0 (docs/29 §16).
# AI_PRICE_INPUT_PER_MTOK=
# AI_PRICE_OUTPUT_PER_MTOK=
